This crate is a Rust implementation of Real-ESRGAN's compact network,
provided under MIT. It reproduces the results of the project below, measured
by running it. The engines under it (crates/native-engine and
crates/native-vulkan) and the work they build on are credited in the
repository's NOTICE.

1. Real-ESRGAN (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2021 Xintao Wang), by Xintao
   Wang, Liangbin Xie, Chao Dong and Ying Shan: "Real-ESRGAN: Training
   Real-World Blind Super-Resolution with Pure Synthetic Data", ICCV
   Workshops, 2021. https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN
   The network (SRVGGNetCompact), its weights realesr-general-x4v3 and
   realesr-general-wdn-x4v3 (published with it in the v0.2.5.0 release) and
   the reference outputs it is checked against. The two weight sets are
   blended as in Xintao Wang, Ke Yu, Chao Dong, Xiaoou Tang and Chen Change
   Loy, "Deep Network Interpolation for Continuous Imagery Effect
   Transition", CVPR 2019. tools/realesrgan/torch_reference.py restates the network's
   PyTorch class from realesrgan/archs/srvgg_arch.py. No weights are
   included: tools/realesrgan/export_weights.py converts checkpoints that you obtain
   yourself. The weights files it writes are modified from them (two
   checkpoints blended, matrices reordered) and stay under Real-ESRGAN's
   BSD-3-Clause licence (notice A), whose text has to travel with any of them
   you redistribute.


A. Real-ESRGAN, https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN, the licence of its
   weights

